            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0826" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23380/10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: Referring to the
                    correspondence this embassy has had the honor to exchange with the Department of
                    State on the subject of the celebration of the centennial of our independence, I
                    take pleasure in informing your excellency that the dates of September 6 and 7
                    next have been set for the reception of the ambassadors and envoys of the
                    Governments who will honor us with their attendance at the festivities.</p>
                <p>Our minister of foreign relations would, therefore, be very glad if the delegates
                    were in Mexico on the 5th of that month.</p>
                <p>I further have the honor to apprise your excellency that on that occasion the
                    said ambassadors and envoys will take precedence according to the date of their
                    arrival in Mexican territory.</p>
                <p>I take, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. L. de la
                    Barra.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
